  "problem": "Model choice could treat model output as gold, leak held-out labels into prompts, call live OpenRouter, or let cheap tokens and inter-model agreement override the \u22650.98 precision / zero critical-error gate. A failed model gate could be treated as disabling deterministic collection.",
  "resulting_behavior": "C-027-1 freezes independently adjudicated CMS/CDC/Census/unit/date/insufficient-evidence tasks with critical-error categories and reviewer disagreement. Public prompts exclude held-out labels. Model output is not gold. C-027-2 compares exact IDs deepseek/deepseek-chat and meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor on recorded offline outputs under the editable $10 pilot configuration, saving tokens, actual price, latency, abstentions and rejected claims. The offline harness works without credentials. --live reports exact model/endpoint and total spend without HTTP. C-027-3 reports precision, coverage, critical errors and review cost. A model failing a task class is disabled for that class. Cheap tokens and agreement do not override the gate. Neither recorded model is publication-eligible on this fixture. Deterministic collection remains operational. R14 remains unaccepted.",
